      "<p>New York apartments do not keep a steady climate. Steam radiators dry the air in January. Window units and central AC drop it again in July. Cooking, dishwashers, and showers spike it in between. Catalog faces do not age the same way in that cycle.</p>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY specs painted doors, real wood veneer, and durable laminate faces by appointment in Brooklyn, Manhattan, and Queens. We are home-based in Bushwick &mdash; not a walk-in showroom at 10 Montieth. Related: <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/wood-species-kitchen-cabinets-nyc\">wood species for NYC kitchens</a>, the <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/wood-species\">wood species guide</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/shaker-vs-slim-shaker-nyc\">shaker vs slim shaker</a>, and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-closet-systems-long-island-city\">custom closet systems in Long Island City</a>.</p>",
      "<h2>What humidity actually does in an NYC apartment</h2>",
      "<p>Humidity here is a daily swing, not one number:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li><strong>Steam heat</strong> in prewar walk-ups and co-ops pulls moisture out of wood and paint films in winter.</li>",
      "<li><strong>AC cycles</strong> in condos reverse it &mdash; cool dry air after a humid commute does not match the wet kitchen at 7 p.m.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Kitchens</strong> add dishwasher exhaust, boiling pots, and a fridge that sweats on the side panel.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Baths and laundry</strong> sit next to millwork more often than people plan &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-vanity-small-nyc-bathrooms\">small NYC vanities</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-laundry-mudroom-millwork-brooklyn\">Brooklyn laundry / mudroom millwork</a>.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Waterfront and LIC towers</strong> pick up coastal air; older brick does the same through plaster.</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>We do not invent humidity ratings. We specify sealed edges, honest substrates, and faces that match how the room is used. Fillers and scribes still matter.</p>",
      "<h2>Painted MDF and paint-grade doors</h2>",
      "<p>Painted cabinets are the default when the client wants color, not grain: white, putty, sage, navy, black. High-quality MDF or paint-grade maple takes a smooth film that photographs clean in a galley and pairs with <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/shaker-vs-slim-shaker-nyc\">classic or slim shaker</a>. Color stays even across a long run.</p>",
      "<p>Honest tradeoffs: paint shows chips and scuffs more than a mid-tone wood-look laminate. Lower corners next to a dishwasher take the hits. Raw MDF edges swell if standing water sits on an unsealed cut &mdash; we band and seal edges; we do not pretend paint is waterproof. Soft-close hardware reduces slam chips (<a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/soft-close-blum-vs-hettich-nyc\">Blum vs Hettich</a>). We talk touch-up realistically.</p>",
      "<h2>Real wood veneer</h2>",
      "<p>Veneer is a thin slice of real maple, walnut, oak, or similar, pressed onto a stable core. You get genuine grain without a solid-lumber door that cups across a 24-inch slab. Species notes: <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/wood-species-kitchen-cabinets-nyc\">wood species kitchen cabinets NYC</a> and the <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/wood-species\">species page</a>. Walnut and white oak read as furniture in a small <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-park-slope-brownstones\">Park Slope</a> or <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-astoria-queens\">Astoria</a> galley.</p>",
      "<p>Honest tradeoffs: veneer still moves with the core and the finish. Poorly sealed edges and backs let moisture in. Open-pore oak holds kitchen grease if the finish is thin. We do not leave raw walnut next to a range. Veneer is right when the client wants real wood in the sightline and will wipe it like furniture. It is wrong next to a steamy bath with no exhaust.</p>",
      "<h2>Durable laminates and wood-look systems</h2>",
      "<p>Engineered faces are not a downgrade when specified honestly. Melamine and high-pressure laminates stay flatter across wide doors, wipe clean, and lock a consistent color across a long run. Systems we already use &mdash; <strong>Tafisa, Egger, Shinnoki, Wilsonart, AGT</strong> &mdash; cover oak, walnut, and painted-look colors without waiting on lumber that may check.</p>",
      "<p>We use the same language on <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-closet-systems-long-island-city\">LIC closets</a>: painted MDF scuffs; durable laminate wipes. Kitchens, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-pantry-millwork-nyc\">pantries</a>, and closet interiors often share one face. Laminates earn their keep in top-floor walk-ups, kitchens next to laundry, slab doors, and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-bathroom-vanity-nyc\">bath vanities</a> that see splash. Skip them when the client wants grain that changes from door to door.</p>",
      "<h2>What we specify, room by room</h2>",
      "<p>We do not pick one finish for every job:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li><strong>Kitchens</strong> &mdash; paint-grade for color galleys; veneer when walnut or oak is the point; Tafisa / Egger / Shinnoki / Wilsonart / AGT when wipeability and flat slabs matter. <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/dovetail-drawer-boxes-nyc-kitchens\">Dovetail drawer boxes</a> sit behind any of those faces.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Baths</strong> &mdash; durable laminate or a well-sealed paint system; keep raw veneer off the wettest edge. The <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/designer\">designer</a> maps vanity layouts; those images are layout previews, not finished photography.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Closets and laundry</strong> &mdash; wipeable wood-look or solid color panels.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Borough landers</strong> &mdash; same finish logic in <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">Manhattan</a>, and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-queens\">Queens</a>.</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>Finished photography lives on <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/case-studies\">case studies</a> when a client allows photos. We do not invent awards, star ratings, or testimonials. Linear footage, door style, hardware, and finish brand drive cost. Planning ranges wait on a measure. Since 2009 / 15+ years is accurate. More: <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/about\">About</a> and the <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog\">blog</a>.</p>",
      "<h2>How we sequence the finish decision</h2>",
      "<ol>",
      "<li><strong>Scope call</strong> &mdash; kitchen, bath, closet, or mix; borough; steam heat vs central HVAC if you know it.</li>",
