      "<li><strong>Work-hour windows</strong> &mdash; noisy fastening often weekdays only; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/condo-board-kitchen-renovation-rules-nyc\">condo board kitchen renovation rules</a> for the same paperwork culture</li>",
      "<li><strong>Freight and curb</strong> &mdash; reserved elevators, pads, and staging floors</li>",
      "<li><strong>Occupied-unit protection</strong> &mdash; floors, doors, and neighbors stay covered &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/occupied-unit-kitchen-install-logistics-nyc\">occupied-unit install logistics</a></li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>We supply millwork drawings and COI support. We do not invent board approvals. Your GC or you package the building&rsquo;s list.</p>",
      "<h2>Long Island City building types we see often</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Waterfront towers (Hunters Point South, Gantry Plaza area).</strong> Walk-ins with glass, low ceilings at the bulkhead, and strict freight rules. Measure sprinkler clearances before you lock a double-hang elevation.</p>",
