      "<p><strong>Older brick walk-ups near Vernon and Broadway.</strong> Reach-ins that need scribed side panels and shorter towers to clear stair landings. Same Queens context as <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-astoria-queens\">Astoria kitchen cabinets</a>.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Brooklyn and Manhattan spillover.</strong> Same shop, same process &mdash; <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-closet-millwork-brooklyn\">Brooklyn closets</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/reach-in-closet-millwork-manhattan-coops\">Manhattan reach-ins</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">Manhattan kitchens</a>. We measure by appointment. Samples come to you. No public showroom floor.</p>",
      "<h2>How we sequence a Long Island City closet system</h2>",
      "<ol>",
      "<li><strong>Scope call</strong> &mdash; walk-in vs reach-in, hang vs drawers, borough, board rules you already know.</li>",
      "<li><strong>On-site measure</strong> &mdash; widths, depths, bulkheads, outlets, door swing, and the delivery path.</li>",
