      "<p>Brooklyn retail rarely gets a blank white box. You get a storefront with a column in the wrong place, a slab that slopes toward the door, a landlord who wants Class A laminate on anything visible from the corridor, and a freight path that shares the sidewalk shed with three other trades. A catalog reception desk assumes square corners and a loading dock. Your lease does not.</p>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY builds reception desks and light commercial millwork by appointment in Brooklyn, Manhattan, and Queens. We are home-based in Bushwick &mdash; not a walk-in showroom at 10 Montieth. This post deepens the <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/commercial-millwork-nyc\">commercial millwork overview</a> for Brooklyn retail: reception desks, cash wraps, and small fixture runs under real landlord rules. Related: <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn kitchens</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-park-slope-brownstones\">Park Slope brownstone kitchens</a>, and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/case-studies\">case studies</a>.</p>",
      "<h2>What &ldquo;light commercial&rdquo; means for a Brooklyn shop</h2>",
      "<p>Light commercial millwork is the furniture-grade casework a boutique, salon, clinic front desk, or small showroom needs to open:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li><strong>Reception / lobby desks</strong> with cable chase, POS cutouts, and ADA knee clearance where required</li>",
      "<li><strong>Cash wraps</strong> with lockable drawers, bag shelf, and a durable work surface</li>",
      "<li><strong>Display pedestals and wall shelving</strong> that mount to studs or masonry without looking like warehouse racking</li>",
      "<li><strong>Back-of-house storage</strong> &mdash; tall cabinets, coat closets, and printer niches that hide ops without eating the sales floor</li>",
      "<li><strong>Small break nooks</strong> for staff &mdash; same cabinet systems as residential, specified for heavier daily wipe-down</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>We do not invent awards or claim design renders are finished installs. Previews are layout tools. Finished photos live on <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/case-studies\">case studies</a> when a client allows them.</p>",
      "<h2>Why stock desks fail in Brooklyn storefronts</h2>",
      "<p>Catalog reception desks assume level floors and a freight elevator into the suite. Brooklyn retail often has out-of-level slabs, cast-iron columns or HVAC soffits that steal depth, narrow storefronts where a deep U-desk blocks the aisle, shared loading that only works before 10am or after close, and landlord finish lists that reject a veneer you already ordered online.</p>",
      "<p>A custom reception desk is measured in the leased space: length against the real wall, depth that still leaves a customer path, height for the POS and standing queue, and panel sizes that fit the freight path or stair. Fillers and scribe strips are designed in &mdash; not improvised with shims on install day.</p>",
      "<h2>Layout moves that make a reception desk usable</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Honest footprint.</strong> Deep enough for a keyboard and bag drop; shallow enough that two people can pass. In a 12-foot-wide boutique, a 30-inch-deep desk can kill the sales floor.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Cable and POS first.</strong> Card readers, printers, and cameras need chase space before the top is laminated. Plan power and data with the electrician; do not drill the finished top after the fact.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Lockable storage.</strong> Soft-close drawers with locks beat open cubbies &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/soft-close-blum-vs-hettich-nyc\">Blum vs Hettich soft-close</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/dovetail-drawer-boxes-nyc-kitchens\">dovetail drawer boxes</a> when you want furniture-grade construction behind the retail face.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Wipeable finishes.</strong> Painted MDF scuffs fast beside a coffee station. Laminate, thermofoil, or durable veneer systems we already use (Tafisa, Egger, Shinnoki, Wilsonart, AGT) survive cleaning better. Match nearby residential language via <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/wood-species\">wood species</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/shaker-vs-slim-shaker-nyc\">shaker vs slim shaker</a> when the brand wants coherence with an upstairs apartment or office.</p>",
      "<p><strong>ADA and standing queues.</strong> Check knee clearance and approach space in the room. Standing-height wraps need a lower transaction bay or side return so shorter customers and wheelchair users are not negotiating over a 42-inch counter.</p>",
      "<h2>Landlord, COI, and after-hours logistics</h2>",
      "<p>Brooklyn retail sits under landlords, BIDs, and sometimes condo boards above the storefront. Expect:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li><strong><a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/certificate-of-insurance-kitchen-remodel-nyc\">Certificate of Insurance</a></strong> naming the landlord and management company exactly as written on the lease</li>",
      "<li><strong>Work-hour windows</strong> &mdash; noisy fastening often limited weekdays; many shops prefer install after close</li>",
      "<li><strong>Freight and curb</strong> &mdash; shared freight and sidewalk sheds need a measured path on day one &mdash; same discipline as <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/freight-elevator-kitchen-cabinet-delivery-nyc\">freight elevator delivery</a></li>",
      "<li><strong>Occupied-space protection</strong> &mdash; finished floors, glass, and neighboring tenants stay covered &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/occupied-unit-kitchen-install-logistics-nyc\">occupied-unit install logistics</a></li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>We supply millwork drawings and COI support. We do not invent landlord approvals. Your GC or you package the building&rsquo;s list.</p>",
      "<h2>Brooklyn neighborhoods and storefront types</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Williamsburg / Greenpoint / Bushwick.</strong> Narrow storefronts and loft conversions that want a reception desk that looks residential-clean, not corporate beige. Measure carefully around columns and exposed brick.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Park Slope / Cobble Hill / Carroll Gardens.</strong> Street-level retail under residential &mdash; quiet hours matter when the freight path shares a residential building. Kitchen clients in the same zip often start from <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-park-slope-brownstones\">Park Slope kitchen cabinets</a> or <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn kitchens</a>.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Downtown Brooklyn / DUMBO / Industry City.</strong> Newer shells with cleaner slabs but stricter landlord finish and insurance packages. Still measure the freight path.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Queens and Manhattan spillover.</strong> Same shop, same process &mdash; <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-queens\">Queens kitchens</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-kitchen-cabinets-astoria-queens\">Astoria kitchens</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">Manhattan kitchens</a>. We measure by appointment. Samples come to the lease. No public showroom floor.</p>",
      "<h2>How we sequence a Brooklyn retail reception desk</h2>",
      "<ol>",
      "<li><strong>Scope call</strong> &mdash; desk vs cash wrap, length and height, POS needs, borough, landlord rules you already know.</li>",
      "<li><strong>On-site measure</strong> &mdash; walls, columns, slab level, outlets, door swing, and the delivery path.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Shop drawings</strong> &mdash; plan, elevation, sections, finish schedule, lock hardware, cable chase notes.</li>",
