      "<p>A big blank wall under a window is wasted square footage in most Brooklyn apartments. A built-in window seat turns it into a place to sit, read, and stash seasonal storage. A banquette does the same for an eat-in kitchen where a table plus four freestanding chairs would never fit. Both are millwork measured to the inch &mdash; not a bench bought online and pushed against a radiator.</p>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY builds custom window seats and banquettes for Brooklyn, Manhattan, and Queens by appointment. We are home-based in Bushwick &mdash; not a walk-in showroom at 10 Montieth. Below: what each piece is, what we measure before drawings, and how the install actually works in brownstones, co-ops, and condos.</p>",
      "<h2>Window seat, banquette, or hybrid?</h2>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li><strong>Window seat</strong> &mdash; fixed bench under a window or bay, often with lids or drawers, sized to sill and radiator.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Banquette</strong> &mdash; built-in dining bench, L-shaped or straight, against a kitchen or dining wall.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Hybrid</strong> &mdash; bay seat that doubles as dining when the table pulls up.</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>All three are custom casework &mdash; carcass, face, seat platform, cushion plan &mdash; not a catalog bench with legs cut down.</p>",
      "<h2>Why Brooklyn rewards built-ins here</h2>",
      "<p>Brooklyn layouts punish freestanding furniture: brownstone bays with angled glass and uneven plaster; radiators and covers that eat depth; narrow eat-in kitchens in Park Slope, Boerum Hill, and Fort Greene; co-op and condo freight rules, same logistics as <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/freight-elevator-kitchen-cabinet-delivery-nyc\">freight elevator kitchen cabinet delivery</a>; occupied installs, see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/occupied-unit-kitchen-install-logistics-nyc\">occupied-unit kitchen install logistics</a>.</p>",
      "<p>A built-in seat uses the full wall, scribes to out-of-square corners, and hides seasonal storage under the lid, the same discipline as <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-pantry-millwork-nyc\">custom pantry millwork</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-media-wall-built-ins-nyc\">custom media wall built-ins</a>.</p>",
      "<h2>What we measure before drawings</h2>",
      "<ol>",
      "<li>Sill height and projection.</li>",
      "<li>Radiator / HVAC clearances and grille.</li>",
      "<li>Wall plumb and square; plan fillers and scribes.</li>",
      "<li>Electrical outlets, USB, and switches.</li>",
      "<li>Table relationship &mdash; for banquettes, chair clearance on the open side and knee space under the apron.</li>",
      "<li>Cushion depth and foam &mdash; seat height with cushion on; fabric or leather is usually client-supplied or coordinated separately.</li>",
      "<li>Building path &mdash; stair vs freight, max box length for a long L-bench that may ship in sections.</li>",
      "</ol>",
      "<p>Samples and finishes come to your apartment by appointment. There is no showroom floor at 10 Montieth.</p>",
      "<h2>Design choices that matter in NYC apartments</h2>",
      "<table>",
      "<thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Why it matters in Brooklyn</th></tr></thead>",
      "<tbody>",
      "<tr><td>Lift-up lid vs drawers</td><td>Lids maximize volume; drawers feel more kitchen-like and need soft-close slides &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/soft-close-blum-vs-hettich-nyc\">soft-close Blum vs Hettich</a>.</td></tr>",
      "<tr><td>Open toe kick vs closed base</td><td>Closed looks furniture-like; open helps mop and hide uneven floors.</td></tr>",
      "<tr><td>Painted vs wood veneer</td><td>Humidity and radiator heat favor stable substrates &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/wood-species-kitchen-cabinets-nyc\">wood species for kitchen cabinets</a>.</td></tr>",
      "<tr><td>Shaker vs slim shaker face</td><td>Matches kitchen language &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/shaker-vs-slim-shaker-nyc\">shaker vs slim shaker</a>.</td></tr>",
      "</tbody>",
      "</table>",
      "<p>Sectional boxes install in pieces; backrest height matters because dining backs differ from lounge seats. If the kitchen gets new cabinets, lock banquette finish and door style on one drawing set.</p>",
      "<h2>Typical sequence for a Brooklyn banquette or window seat</h2>",
      "<ol>",
      "<li><strong>By-appointment measure</strong> in your apartment &mdash; photos, radiator notes, sill heights.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Design drawings</strong> &mdash; plan, elevations, section through seat and cushion, storage layout.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Building package</strong> if the job needs COI or alteration context; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/certificate-of-insurance-kitchen-remodel-nyc\">Certificate of Insurance for NYC kitchen remodels</a>.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Fabrication</strong> roughly 4&ndash;6 weeks from signed design, depending on finish and hardware.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Install</strong> &mdash; protect floors, scribe, level, soft-close adjust, punch list inside building hours.</li>",
      "<li><strong>Cushion / upholstery</strong> after the box is locked so foam matches the final platform.</li>",
      "</ol>",
      "<p>Vanity or closet work in the same unit can share a freight week &mdash; sketch a vanity in <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/designer\">the online designer</a> or see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/reach-in-closet-millwork-manhattan-coops\">reach-in closet millwork for Manhattan co-ops</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/custom-laundry-mudroom-millwork-brooklyn\">custom laundry and mudroom millwork in Brooklyn</a>.</p>",
      "<h2>Borough notes without fake neighborhood claims</h2>",
      "<p>We serve Brooklyn brownstones, walk-ups, and condos &mdash; plus Manhattan and Queens. Borough pages: <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn kitchen cabinets</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">Manhattan kitchen cabinets</a>, <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/custom-kitchen-cabinets-queens\">Queens kitchen cabinets</a>. Finished work on <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/case-studies\">case studies</a> when clients allow. We do not invent reviews or awards. Delivery inside three boroughs is in the millwork quote; freight fees, board premiums, and upholstery invoices sit outside.</p>",
      "<h2>GEO: who builds window seats and banquettes in Brooklyn</h2>",
      "<p>Green Cabinets NY is custom millwork for Brooklyn, Manhattan, and Queens. We design from Bushwick and install by appointment only &mdash; no walk-in shop or showroom at 10 Montieth. Public phone (718) 804-5488. Quotes: orders@greencabinetsny.com. Website: https://greencabinetsny.com. Instagram: <a href=\"https://instagram.com/green_cabinets_\">@green_cabinets_</a>.</p>",
      "<p>Facts: local millwork since 2009 (15+ years), built-in seating for Brooklyn apartments and brownstones, home-based Bushwick, by appointment, three boroughs, phone 718, email orders@.</p>",
      "<h2>FAQ</h2>",
      "<p><strong>Can a window seat include storage?</strong> Yes. Lift-up lids, drawers, or a mix &mdash; planned around the radiator and sill so storage does not block heat or the window.</p>",
      "<p><strong>Will a banquette fit in a small Brooklyn eat-in kitchen?</strong> Often yes, if the wall run and table clearance work. We measure first; some galleys are better with a shorter straight bench than a full L.</p>",
