      "<p>Matching an existing china cabinet or built-in door profile is a real ask here. Bring photos or a molding sample; we draw the match into shop drawings before fabrication &mdash; not a stock door &ldquo;close enough&rdquo; swap.</p>",
      "<h2>Co-ops and condos on Prospect Park West and Seventh Avenue</h2>",
      "<p>Park Slope is not only single-family brownstones. Pre-war co-ops and condos along Prospect Park West, Eighth, and Seventh Avenue add COI, alteration paperwork, work hours, hallway protection, and freight booking when available. Rules vary by board. This is not legal advice. You own board submissions; we support with drawings and COI when asked.</p>",
      "<p>Delivery follows our NYC install playbook &mdash; see <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/nyc-kitchen-cabinet-installation\">kitchen installation in NYC</a> and <a href=\"https://greencabinetsny.com/blog/freight-elevator-kitchen-cabinet-delivery-nyc\">freight elevator delivery</a>. Occupied-unit installs get floor protection and quiet-hours discipline.</p>",
      "<h2>How a Park Slope kitchen project usually runs</h2>",
