      "<p>A Queens kitchen is almost never the box a warehouse SKU was cut for. An Astoria walk-up galley is 9 feet long and 6 feet wide, with a radiator eating a corner. A Forest Hills co-op has 8-foot-4 ceilings, so a 48-inch upper will not fit. An LIC tower has a bulkhead, a sprinkler, and a dock that wants a COI before the cart rolls in. Stock cabinets paper over that with filler. Custom millwork is built to the opening.</p>",
