      "<p>A Manhattan kitchen is rarely just cabinets. It is a building. Co-ops want a certificate of insurance before anyone rolls a cart into the lobby. Condos want quiet hours, elevator pads, and a finish schedule that matches the alteration agreement. Stock boxes ignore that. Custom millwork plans for it.</p>",
