      "<li>Shared plumbing stacks that limit where the sink and dishwasher can move</li>",
      "<li>Building rules on work hours, dust, and how material enters the freight elevator</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>That is why <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-manhattan\">custom kitchen cabinets in Manhattan</a> are a millwork job, not a warehouse pickup. The same logic applies for <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-brooklyn\">Brooklyn</a> brownstones and <a href=\"/custom-kitchen-cabinets-queens\">Queens</a> apartments: measure the real room, then build.</p>",
      "<h2>COI and building logistics (before we cut a truck)</h2>",
      "<p>Most Manhattan co-ops and many condos will not let installers on site without paperwork. We plan that early so the job does not stall in the lobby.</p>",
      "<p>Typical building asks:</p>",
      "<ul>",
      "<li>Certificate of insurance (COI) naming the co-op or condo and often the managing agent</li>",
      "<li>Work hours (often weekday mornings through mid-afternoon, no weekend noise)</li>",
      "<li>Elevator reservation and protective pads</li>",
      "<li>Sometimes a building-approved alteration package or architect stamp for larger moves</li>",
      "</ul>",
      "<p>We install by appointment. There is no customer-facing shop. Quotes start with photos, rough sizes, and the borough. Email <a href=\"mailto:orders@greencabinetsny.com\">orders@greencabinetsny.com</a> or call <a href=\"tel:+17188045488\">(718) 804-5488</a> with name, email, phone, and whether the building is a co-op or condo. If you already have the alteration agreement, send that too.</p>",
      "<h2>Door styles and finishes that hold up in small kitchens</h2>",
      "<p>Styles we spec often: classic shaker, slim shaker, slab, and glass uppers when a dark galley needs borrowed light. Finishes: painted whites, soft sage, navy, putty, and wood tones in walnut or white oak. Hardware in unlacquered brass, matte black, or brushed nickel. See <a href=\"/wood-species\">wood species</a>.</p>",
